*Heading
** Measures the stiffness Abaqus uses for contact-based cohesive behaviour when
** *COHESIVE BEHAVIOR is given no data line. Two stacked bricks share no nodes at the
** interface, exactly as the plate model's plies do not, so the opening is carried by the
** cohesive interaction alone. The top face is pulled by a slow prescribed displacement,
** twenty microseconds against a 0.39 us axial period, so the response is quasi-static and
** the opening can be read without the bricks ringing. Write the same deck with and without
** a data line under *COHESIVE BEHAVIOR and the two stiffnesses fall out of
** K = (reaction force / area) / opening.
