** The lateral degrees of freedom are held on both faces either side of the interface and
** on the pulled face. Without that the upper brick is free to tilt, the interface opens
** as a wedge and the opening read is the wedge's maximum rather than the value the
** stiffness belongs to; the first run of this deck measured 2.9 times the default against
** the specified value for exactly that reason.
